exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > book, eulogy, chronicle and village name prompts (P9.5) 1`] = `
"Write a little book that Krikwick wrote for the village, in Krikwick's own voice.
First line: "Title: " and a short title of at most 6 words. Then one page of at most 120 words on how to make or know these things:
Club: wood and stone
that redcaps are poison
About Krikwick: adult, brave, greedy; feeling proud."
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > book, eulogy, chronicle and village name prompts (P9.5) 2`] = `
"Fizz speaks at the funeral of Krikwick. Write what Fizz says: 2-4 sentences, warm and simple.
About Krikwick: Krikwick the Brave, lived 4 seasons, died: old age. Family: Mib (child).
What Fizz remembers of Krikwick:
Krikwick slew a Gnasher
About Fizz: adult, shy, curious; Krikwick was to them: best friend."
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > book, eulogy, chronicle and village name prompts (P9.5) 3`] = `
"Krikwick, the eldest goblin of Toadmire, writes the chronicle of the Spring of year 1: one saga paragraph of 120-200 words, in the chronicler's voice.
The season in numbers: 8 goblins at its start, 9 at its end; 2 hatched, 1 died; 3 buildings finished; 1 new things worked out.
What happened:
day 2 — I slew a Gnasher
From the diaries:
Fizz: Today was muddy."
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > book, eulogy, chronicle and village name prompts (P9.5) 4`] = `
"The goblins' village has grown to 3 huts and needs a name. Invent one: one or two words with goblin flavor, fitting the land. Answer with the name only.
Places nearby: Sad Pond, Star Hollow. Chief: Grubnok."
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > diary, dialogue and bark prompts 1`] = `
"Write Krikwick's diary entry for today, in first person, 40-90 words.
About Krikwick: adult, 3 seasons old, small and dark mossy green. Personality: brave, greedy.
Known as: Krikwick the Brave.
Traits: scarred. Feeling: proud. Biggest worry: sleep.
Relationships: Fizz (best friend); Grubnok (rival).
Season: Autumn, weather: rain. Chief: Grubnok.
Today:
dawn — I picked apple ×4
dusk — I slew a Gnasher at Sad Pond
dusk — Fizz was hurt at Sad Pond"
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > diary, dialogue and bark prompts 2`] = `
"Write a short conversation between Krikwick and Fizz, chatting about danger.
2-6 lines. Start every line with the speaker's name and a colon, like "Krikwick: ...". At most 80 characters a line.
Krikwick: adult, brave, greedy; feeling proud; sees Fizz as: best friend. On their mind: dusk — I slew a Gnasher at Sad Pond.
Fizz: adult, shy, curious; feeling worried; sees Krikwick as: best friend. On their mind: none.
Season: Autumn, weather: rain."
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > diary, dialogue and bark prompts 3`] = `
"Write one short line, at most 12 words, that Krikwick calls out right now.
About Krikwick: adult, brave, greedy; feeling proud.
What just happened: I slew a Gnasher"
`;

exports[`prompts (§19.5, P9.3) > system prompt in both languages 1`] = `
"You write short in-character text for a cozy simulation game about small goblins called Nibblets.
Nibblets are earnest, simple-minded, a bit greedy for shiny things, brave in groups, and love apples.
Speak in plain, vivid language with goblin flavor (simple words, occasional made-up goblin
expressions like "grub-gob!" or "by the big apple"). Never mention being an AI or a game.
Use only the names, places and events provided; do not invent new characters or events.
Write in English. No markdown, no lists, no quotation marks around the whole text."
`;
